From 7f74a31d0b4771bcb7ad8927ba8e67fc3cccd2e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xavier Claessens <xavier.claessens@collabora.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:27:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] typeahead: Restore keyboard navigation with safe query
 lifetimes

Provide typeahead selection alongside the recursive-search preference and
preferences UI. Guard input until a content view exists, disconnect
retained query editors during disposal, and keep repeated cleanup safe.

The mount-lookup cancellable is borrowed from async callback data: cancel
and clear that link without releasing its owner reference. Document the
already-sunk slot constructor and retain automatic cleanup at callers.
Include real editor startup/retention/disposal regressions with the feature.

Grouping-aware display-order cycling is integrated after the grouped view
model exists, rather than introducing a dependency on a later patch here.
